ck people say you know to what  purpose  should we open this you know what do we  gain by it they've been something like  2,000 books written about it one  hesitates to crawl into that thicket  because a lot of them are bizarre  notions but if you sort through the  evidence it's hard to conclude that it's  impossible to conclude I think that that  Oswald was acting alone we have I have  seen there's a brood of film one of my  partners represented them and I actually  sat and watched the actual film of it  and you look at that and you can't you  can't believe that it was one person  acting alone you see and going like this  you see them going back it if you see  the real thing as opposed to the few  segments that most people have seen it's  almost impossible and then when you put  that together with the acoustical  evidence that the house assassination  committee came up with and the  circumstantial evidence of the people  five people who were who were  interviewed but later evidence that  comes from the Cuban records from the  CIA records that have been disclosed the  wiretaps that were put together by the  house assassination committee all of it  builds kind of circumstantial evidence  that I think is irresistible points to  the conclusion that that there were more  people than Oz well there and and those  people were either the mob or Cubans who  were being used by the mob  don't you think there's some value them  in having the American population say or  believe in a more common way that Oswald  didn't act on if you ask the person on  the street who killed Kennedy the person  will probably say Oswald but given all  this evidence and given all the reports  that are available to people and and the  voice the heights and so many people's  heads it it was impossible he acted  alone no matter who his partners were  don't you think it's valuable for people  to ultimately say Kennedy was killed by  Oswald and I think if we had a little  more decisive information about w